# Template of <private dir>/compose.env, the environment of the container (env_file of the service).
# Copy this file to <private dir>/compose.env and give the copy the mode 600.
# Paste the key value into the copy. Never put a value into this example.
# Do not give this file to --env-file. The file of --env-file is seat.env.
# See docs/guides/modules.md, component codex-accounts, for the gateway.
# Leave both lines empty if you do not use a gateway.
# The compose-plan action always sets a gateway.

# The gateway key. The entrypoint writes its value to /run/tenant-pi-seat/gateway-key for the seat account.
# Leave it empty when the provider has a native login.
# Put the value between single quotes: Compose interpolates $, and an unquoted " #" starts a comment.
TENANTEXT_LITELLM_API_KEY=''
# The gateway URL, the value of endpoints.codex-accounts in the overlay. It ends in /v1. It is not a secret.
# The launcher of the profile has the URL from the overlay. This line gives it to a process that the container starts.
# This line is optional: a login session does not see the environment of the container.
TENANTEXT_LITELLM_BASE_URL=
